   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor customer
   * @x-autobe-specification Load the wishlist by id and verify that it belongs to the authenticated customer. Reconcile the wishlist item set according to the request body using the wishlist_items table, preserving the wishlist header row. Enforce the unique [wishlist_id, product_id] constraint so each product appears at most once. Reject or ignore product ids that do not exist or have been deleted, depending on the request contract used by the implementation layer, but never leave the wishlist in a partially updated state.
   *
   * Implement the update transactionally: compute the target product set, delete removed wishlist items, insert newly added ones, and leave existing items intact when still selected. Because deleted products are automatically removed from wishlists, the service should also filter out orphaned saved products before committing. Update the wishlist timestamp on success. If any validation or persistence error occurs, roll back the entire change so the customer's saved list remains unchanged.
